{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"beribboned-spherical-pipit","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nFault-seeding under afa0-2e15 (rival-ammoniacal-crustacean) produced two findings about\n`tests/interfaces/store/test_show_no_stall.py::test_cli_show_complete_or_erroring_under_write_burst`\n(8.17-8.76s local; 10.95-22.63s in CI samples — the largest variance contributor in the\ndefault suite):\n\n1. **It does not detect the regression it is named for.** Seeding F1 (reverting the\n   slim-fetch-ledge, `_RECONVERGE_LOCK_TIMEOUT` 2 -> 15) left this test GREEN. Only the two\n   held-lock tests (`test_ensure_fresh_does_not_stall_on_held_write_lock` and\n   `test_reads_complete_promptly_while_write_lock_is_held`) went RED. The 15s lock wait fits\n   inside this test's 60s per-subprocess harness timeout and `show` still emits a complete\n   record, just slowly.\n2. **Its real, exclusive detection value (seeds F3/F6 — exit 0 with a shape-valid but\n   content-incomplete payload) is deterministic and fires on round 0 / ticket 0.** The F3 run\n   aborted at 20.2s against a 28.9s unseeded baseline, i.e. it failed on the first iteration.\n\nThe test therefore runs 6 rounds x 4 tickets x (edit + show) = 48 CLI subprocesses under\n`REBAR_SYNC_PUSH=always` to detect a fault class the first iteration already catches.\n\n**This ticket does NOT propose deleting the test** — afa0-2e15 proved the generic property does\nnot subsume it (F3/F6 are caught only here). It proposes reducing the storm to what the\nevidence justifies, keeping the oracle.\n\n## Plan\n- Establish, by seeding F3 and F6 at successively lower round counts, the smallest storm that\n  still detects them deterministically (expected: 1-2 rounds).\n- Reduce the round count to that measured floor, leaving assertions untouched.\n- Re-run the full afa0-2e15 seed set (F1-F7) against the reduced test and confirm its\n  detection column is unchanged.\n\n## Testing / Verification\n- Seeds F3 and F6 must still go RED at the reduced round count (repeat >= 5 runs each — the\n  storm is concurrent, so a single green is not evidence of stability).\n- Seeds F2 and F4 must still go RED.\n- Unseeded: GREEN over >= 10 consecutive runs (guard against introducing flakiness).\n- Record before/after wall-clock on macOS and in CI.\n- `make lint`, `make typecheck`, `make test`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The reduced test detects every fault class it detected before (F2, F3, F4, F6).\n- [ ] Detection of F3 and F6 is shown stable across repeated runs, not a single sample.\n- [ ] The test is not deleted and its assertions are not weakened.\n- [ ] Measured wall-clock reduction is recorded for macOS.\n- [ ] Measured wall-clock reduction is recorded for CI/Ubuntu.\n- [ ] No new flakiness: >= 10 consecutive unseeded GREEN runs.","id":"ce38-2914-d2f4-4826","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["ci","test-runtime","concurrency"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Right-size the show-under-write-burst storm: 6 rounds buy no detection over round 0"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787172740845683001,"uuid":"81ff9058-3a29-4ca1-9874-b8664aa0db9e"}